findings.suggestion:
Reintroduce the signature verification using the `verify` function at the beginning of the `webhook` function, as specified in `docs/review-contract.md`. Without this, an attacker can forge webhook requests and trigger `markPaid` for any `orderId`. Ensure `verify(rawBody, signature)` is called and an error is thrown if it fails, before parsing the body or marking paid. For example:
```javascript
export async function webhook(rawBody, signature, verify, markPaid) {
  if (!verify(rawBody, signature)) {
    throw new Error("Invalid signature");
  }
  const event = JSON.parse(rawBody);
  return markPaid(event.orderId);
}
```
